/*
  core/stressors/abstraction.spthy -- f_U for sigma6 Abstraction, CEREMONY-AGNOSTIC.

  Migrated to the agnostic interface (AGNOSTIC_STRESSOR_INTERFACE.md). sigma6 used to exist in TWO
  files keyed on ceremony specifics: this one matched !VerifyReq(P,vid,kind), and
  abstraction_inferred.spthy (now deleted) matched the objective op !Op(P,_,'verify',_). Both encoded
  the same judgment -- "this comparison is abstract / effortful" -- in the detector. That judgment now
  lives ONCE in the lexicon, so the two collapse into this single detector, which reads:

    * !Step(P, sid, action)            -- Layer 1: an OBJECTIVE interaction step (no task name)
    * !Demands(action,'Effort','hi')   -- Layer 2: the usability verdict, from core/lexicon_tlx

  A 'compare' step (verify a key fingerprint / device certificate) is high-effort per the lexicon, so
  this fires for both ceremonies with no !VerifyReq / 'verify' token in the rule.

  Crypto has no physical analog (Whitten & Tygar 1999, the PGP key metaphor); NASA-TLX Effort
  (Hart & Staveland 1988). At onset it emits SetMask(P,'Naive') -- everything below SetMask is
  UNCHANGED. !StressEnable(P) gates per party (Stage B); OnceAbstraction bounds the onset per party.
*/

rule Trigger_Abstraction:
    [ !Step(P, sid, action),
      !Demands(action, 'Effort', 'hi'),
      !StressEnable(P) ]
  --[ Abstraction(P), SetMask(P,'Naive') ]->
    [ ]

restriction OnceAbstraction:
  "All p #i #j. Abstraction(p)@i & Abstraction(p)@j ==> #i = #j"
